# ==============================================================================
# Title Music from A Clockwork Orange (1971) - Wendy Carlos & Rachel Elkind
# Based on Music for the Funeral of Queen Mary (1695, Z. 860) by Henry Purcell
# Duration: 2:21 (141 seconds) | Tempo: 60 BPM (M 60 16) | Key: C minor / C Major
#
# Load:   [title_music_clockwork_orange.sk] /ls
# Start:  play        Stop:  stop
# ==============================================================================
# Wendy Carlos & Henry Purcell Historical & Sonic Architecture:
#   1. Exact Baroque Score (Henry Purcell, Z. 860, 1695):
#      Authentic 4-part brass chorale (flat trumpets and sackbuts) across 15 bars:
#      Bar 1: C Major (solemn Picardy third opening)
#      Bar 2: F minor (characteristic English Baroque weeping slide trill)
#      Bar 3: C Major | Bar 4: C minor
#      Bar 5: Ab Major suspension | Bar 6: G Major (Dominant V)
#      Bar 7: G minor | Bar 8: C minor -> D Major secondary dominant
#      Bar 9: G minor | Bar 10: Eb Major relative major
#      Bar 11: F minor -> Bb Major | Bar 12: Eb Major
#      Bar 13: C minor | Bar 14: ii-dim -> G Major authentic cadence
#      Bar 15: C Major grand Picardy third cadence resolution.
#   2. Moog Wavetable Architecture:
#      Moog DWGS band-limited sawtooth (w15) for warm analog brass leads,
#      and Moog DWGS square/pulse (w16) for resonant sub-bass.
#   3. Percussion Section:
#      - Timpani: Layered built-in drum wavetable mallet (w82 f260 a5)
#        and deep sub-sine body (w0 a2) playing the authentic Purcell cadence.
#      - Funeral Side Snare: Built-in drum wavetable (w83 f440 a6)
#        playing crisp military march rolls and cadence flams.
#   4. Rachel Elkind Vocoder / Resonant Formant Choir:
#      In Statement 2, upper-octave synthesizer choir voices (w15 through
#      resonant formants ~950 Hz, 750 Hz, 550 Hz) double the chorale.
#   5. Unified Instrument Command `i` & Sentinels:
#      Uses Skode unified note/articulation command `i` with Note-On,
#      Sustained Ties (.), Rests (-), and Legato Slurs (~Note).
#   6. Structure & Timing:
#      Intro (0:00 - 0:16) -> Statement 1 (0:16 - 1:16) ->
#      Statement 2 (1:16 - 2:16) -> Coda & Cathedral Decay (2:16 - 2:21).
# ==============================================================================

M 60 16

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. CATHEDRAL ACOUSTIC DELAY BUS
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DS 1 60 0.50
DL 1 - - 8 0 0 10
DD 1 8 2

# Auto-cleanup when song ends
[O DQ] /ceb 4 99
/cer 1

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. VOICE ARCHITECTURE: PERCUSSION
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Voice 0: Timpani Mallet Strike
# Built-in drum wavetable w82 tuned to 260 Hz for authoritative high-impact attack
v0
w82 f260 a5 p0 r1 ds.25
[timpani mallet] vt

# Voice 5: Timpani Sub-Bass Resonant Body
# Tuned pure sine wave (w0) providing the resonant 65 Hz / 49 Hz acoustic decay
v5
w0 a2 p0 r1 ds.25
.005 .40 0 .30 t
[timpani sub] vt

# Voice 1: Military Funeral Side Snare
# Built-in drum wavetable w83 tuned for crisp muffled military march rolls
v1
w83 f440 a6 p0 r1 ds.20
[funeral snare] vt

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. VOICE ARCHITECTURE: MOOG BRASS QUARTET
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Voice 10: Soprano Trumpet 1 (Lead Melody)
# Moog-ish band-limited saw (w15) with 24dB ladder filter bite and portamento
v10
w15 a-7 p-0.2 k2800 q1.8 g0.035 r1 ds.30
.010 .25 .70 .22 t
[moog trumpet lead] vt

# Voice 11: Alto Trumpet 2 (Counter-Melody)
# Moog-ish band-limited saw (w15) with rich warm counterpoint
v11
w15 a-8 p0.2 k2400 q1.6 g0.035 r1 ds.30
.012 .28 .65 .22 t
[moog trumpet alto] vt

# Voice 12: Tenor Trombone (Harmonic Core)
# Moog-ish band-limited saw (w15) filling out the solemn Baroque chords
v12
w15 a-8 p-0.3 k1900 q1.5 g0.040 r1 ds.30
.015 .30 .65 .25 t
[moog trombone tenor] vt

# Voice 13: Bass Trombone / Serpent (Walking Bass Foundation)
# Deep resonant Moog low-end brass
v13
w15 a-6 p0.3 k1300 q2.0 g0.040 r1 ds.30
.015 .32 .70 .28 t
[moog brass bass] vt

# Voice 14: Sub Serpent Bass (Sub-Octave Doubling)
# Moog-ish band-limited square/pulse (w16) providing thick analog weight
v14
w16 a-8 p0 k500 q1.2 g0.040 r1 ds.20
.015 .32 .70 .28 t
[sub serpent bass] vt

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. VOICE ARCHITECTURE: RACHEL ELKIND VOCODER CHOIR
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Voice 16: Vocoder Soprano (Ah Formant ~950 Hz, w15 Moog saw carrier)
v16
w15 a-11 p-0.15 k950 q3.5 g0.045 r1 ds.40
.035 .35 .75 .30 t
[vocoder soprano ah] vt

# Voice 17: Vocoder Alto (Oh Formant ~750 Hz, w15 Moog saw carrier)
v17
w15 a-11 p0.15 k750 q3.2 g0.045 r1 ds.40
.035 .35 .75 .30 t
[vocoder alto oh] vt

# Voice 18: Vocoder Tenor (Ah/Mmm Formant ~550 Hz, w15 Moog saw carrier)
v18
w15 a-12 p0 k550 q3.0 g0.045 r1 ds.40
.035 .35 .75 .30 t
[vocoder tenor] vt

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. VOICE ARCHITECTURE: OPENING GLISSANDI
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Voice 20: High Descending Glissando (C6 down to C4, w15 Moog saw)
v20
w15 a-18 p-0.3 k1600 q1.5 g0.15 r1 ds.45
.20 .60 .60 .50 t
[intro gliss high] vt

# Voice 21: Mid Descending Glissando (D5 down to G3, w16 Moog square)
v21
w16 a-19 p0.3 k1200 q1.5 g0.15 r1 ds.45
.20 .60 .60 .50 t
[intro gliss mid] vt

# Voice 22: Low Doom Glissando (C4 down to C2, w15 Moog saw)
v22
w15 a-18 p0 k800 q1.8 g0.18 r1 ds.45
.20 .60 .60 .50 t
[intro gliss low] vt

